TASK:{"title":"AERO9500 Preliminary Report (Part 1)","overview":"Plan a simple space mission that benefits Australia and present preliminary design work to guide the full mission assignment. Explain the mission concept and rationale, plan how the assignment will be completed, identify information sources and software, and show evidence of technical progress."}
RUBRIC:[{"id":"C1","name":"Mission concept and rationale — What will it do, who are the users, why is it needed?","weight":40,"max":40,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"A clear and complete description of mission goals, objectives, and requirements. Clearly relates required mission function to users and their needs. References to literature as appropriate."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Sufficient description of mission goals, objectives, and requirements. Identification of users and their needs. Descriptions feature lack of specific details and/or incomplete referencing."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"A poor description with mission goals, objectives and requirements unclear. Insufficient identification of users and their needs."}]},{"id":"C2","name":"Project plan — How you plan to complete the assignment, including either a Gantt chart or a timetable and information sources you plan to use","weight":30,"max":30,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"The plan for project completion is robust and has provision for project variations and contingencies. The plan fits within the narrative set out by the mission concept – the student makes clear why the plan is developed this way in the context of the mission. Appropriate references to information sources are included."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Plan is presented but lacks some detail. However, the plan is enough to believe that the project is feasible."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"Plan is not included or does not have sufficient detail to demonstrate that the project can be completed."}]},{"id":"C3","name":"Preliminary progress — Technical content and evidence of sufficient work done to date","weight":10,"max":10,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"Good preliminary set of results included with brief description and/or interpretation. Clearly on track for completion."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Minor work completed on the project. Results description or interpretation may be insufficient."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"No actual or useful work completed."}]},{"id":"C4","name":"Report presentation","weight":20,"max":20,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"The document follows a clear and logical structure. The report is very easy to read: well-written, with good spelling and grammar, and appropriate language style. All aspects of formatting are consistent throughout the document. Graphical and tabular presentation of data is appropriate, clear and consistent. References in text match reference list (and vice versa) and are cited properly."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Document is not at a professional level but does make use of headings and subheadings to indicate document structure. The report may be difficult to read: writing is just ok, broad idea comes across; spelling and grammar have some flaws, not quite appropriate language style. Although figures and tables are labelled, the formatting is unclear and/or inconsistent to the extent that the reader can lose track of the context when reading. References in text match reference list (and vice versa) and are mostly cited correctly."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"The document is poorly structured, is not coherent or shows a lack of understanding of the purpose of its sections. Much effort is required to read and understand the report: writing is poor, many mistakes with spelling and grammar, and possibly inappropriate language style (e.g. too informal). Presentation is poor to the extent that it impedes reading of the document. Examples include inconsistent formatting, and unlabelled figures or tables. References are either not cited or cited inconsistently."}]}]
MARKING:{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","met":"yes","where":"Mission Concept & Rationale — GBR monitoring satellite, users and need explained with references"},{"id":"R2","met":"partial","where":"Project Plan — launch/orbit/ground control tasks planned, but orbit choice is technically incorrect (geostationary at 600 km)"},{"id":"R3","met":"yes","where":"Project Plan — STK selected ('STK Design', 'STK Simulations'); tutorials 1–4 completed"},{"id":"R4","met":"yes","where":"Image 1 — Gantt chart with weekly tasks and deadlines"},{"id":"R5","met":"partial","where":"Mission Concept & Rationale — four URLs cited, but no explicit list of planned information sources beyond these"},{"id":"R6","met":"partial","where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress — research and STK tutorials done, but no preliminary technical results shown"}],"technical_issues":[{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress (Orbit Specifics)","issue":"A geostationary orbit requires ~35,786 km altitude; a 600 km orbit is LEO and cannot keep the satellite fixed above the reef. Also, GEO coverage of the whole GBR would have poor resolution for seafloor colour detection."},{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","issue":"The 2017 bleaching statistic ('another 50 percent perished') likely misrepresents the source, which referred to northern/central sections, not the entire reef."}],"overall":"Well-motivated, clearly written mission concept benefiting Australia with a detailed Gantt-chart plan and STK selection. Weakened by a fundamental orbit technical error, absence of preliminary results/calculations, and no contingency planning or consolidated source list.","criteria":[{"id":"C1","level":"Accomplished","mark":7.0,"scale":10.0,"points":28.0,"max":40.0,"reasoning":"Clear mission purpose, identified users (marine/conservation scientists), and strong rationale for Australia's GBR, supported by four literature citations. However, explicit mission goals, objectives and quantified requirements are not formally stated, keeping it at the lower end of Accomplished.","evidence":[{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","quote":"A near-real-time relay to monitoring stations on the ground would allow marine and conservation scientists to more accurately predict and react to coral bleaching events."},{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","quote":"Reef-monitoring satellites could also be used to report sea surface temperatures, thermal stress on coral, and bathymetry"}]},{"id":"C2","level":"Adequate","mark":6.0,"scale":10.0,"points":18.0,"max":30.0,"reasoning":"A detailed Gantt chart with week-by-week tasks, deadlines and narrative tying tasks to the mission (launch, orbit, ground control, comms, end-of-life). Fits the mission narrative well, but no provision for contingencies/variations and no consolidated list of planned information sources.","evidence":[{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","quote":"Project work will be divided into weeks via a Gantt Chart. Detailed task descriptions can be found on the next page."},{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","quote":"In addition to my own research, the syllabus work on astrodynamics will help me to understand and design an optimal mission."}]},{"id":"C3","level":"Adequate","mark":4.0,"scale":10.0,"points":4.0,"max":10.0,"reasoning":"Progress consists of literature research and completing four STK tutorials, but no preliminary results, calculations, or STK outputs are presented or interpreted. The stated orbit concept contains a fundamental technical error (see technical issues), indicating early-stage understanding.","evidence":[{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","quote":"I have read the brief of Asner's monitoring system in Hawaii, researched into how coral bleaching occurs and its severity, and also completed STK tutorials 1, 2, 3 & 4."},{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","quote":"My current choice is a geostationary orbit at an altitude of 600 km, which keeps the satellite fixed above the reef at all times."}]},{"id":"C4","level":"Accomplished","mark":7.0,"scale":10.0,"points":14.0,"max":20.0,"reasoning":"Clear logical structure with headings, well-written prose, consistent formatting, and a well-labelled, legible Gantt chart. References are cited in text and match listed URLs, though footnote-style URLs rather than a formal reference list slightly weaken scholarly presentation.","evidence":[{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","quote":"¹ https://www.noaa.gov/education/resource-collections/ocean-coasts/ocean-acidification"},{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","quote":"Completed stages are gold. Incomplete stages are blue. Deadlines are indicated by red lines."}]}]}
